// User Core profile — the base layer every user profile.jsonc is resolved
// over (ADR 0036, ADR 0057). Lists concat+dedupe with the user profile;
// scalars user-wins. A user drops something declared here via
// `programs_exclude`.
//
// `shell` is /bin/zsh: the entire tracked shell payload is zsh while
// .bashrc/.bash_profile/.profile are untracked — so a bash default landed a
// fresh install in a shell whose stowed config never loaded. The zsh package
// itself is NOT declared: ensure_login_shell_installed pacman-installs a
// user's login shell when the binary is missing. Root stays /bin/bash
// (ADR 0054, options.root_shell).
//
// `programs` is the standard tooling every real user gets. The two VM test
// users exclude both — they exercise the system install path, not user
// program installs.
{
  "shell": "/bin/zsh",
  "sudo": false,
  "groups": ["audio", "video", "storage", "optical", "network", "seat"],
  "programs": ["docker", "virt-manager"],
  "ssh_authorized_keys": []
}
